        "summary": "Implemented order state transitions in stockflow/main.py:\n\n1. **POST /orders/{id}/confirm**: Transitions PENDING -> CONFIRMED. Returns 409 INVALID_ORDER_STATE for any other state.\n2. **POST /orders/{id}/ship**: Transitions CONFIRMED -> SHIPPED. Returns 409 INVALID_ORDER_STATE for any other state.\n3. **POST /orders/{id}/cancel**: Transitions PENDING or CONFIRMED -> CANCELED with stock restoration. Returns 409 INVALID_ORDER_STATE for SHIPPED or CANCELED states.\n\nKey design decisions:\n- All state transition endpoints use `lock=True` (row-level locking with `with_for_update()`) to handle concurrent operations safely\n- Stock is only restored on cancel (not on confirm/ship), and only once since the status changes to CANCELED\n- Tenant boundary is maintained through the existing `load_order` helper which filters by `tenant_id`\n- All endpoints follow the existing error handling pattern with ApiError exceptions",
